## Requirements

- Docker and Docker Compose running on the target host
- `community.docker` collection

## Role Variables

Variables follow the pattern `<<gen_role_name>>_<key>` for role-wide settings and `<<gen_role_name>>_<service>_<key>` for per-service settings. Defaults are in `defaults/main/`.

### Role-wide

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `<<gen_role_name>>_project_dir` | Directory on the target host where the Compose project lives |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_composefile` | Path to the rendered `docker-compose.yml` |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_domain` | FQDN for the service (`<<gen_role_name>>.<<gen_role_tld>>` by default) |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_configs` | Dict of config file specs (see Configs below) |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_secrets` | Dict of secret file specs (see Secrets below) |

### Per-service

Each entry in `gen_role_services` gets its own defaults block. Common keys for each service `<svc>`:

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `<<gen_role_name>>_<svc>_image` | Container image |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_<svc>_version` | Image tag |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_<svc>_ports` | Published ports |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_<svc>_volumes` | Volume mounts |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_<svc>_environment` | Environment variables |
| `<<gen_role_name>>_<svc>_restart` | Restart policy |

The `docker-compose.yml.j2` template renders only keys that are non-null, so unused keys can be left at their defaults without appearing in the output.

## Configs

`tasks/configs.yml` manages files in `<<gen_role_name>>_configs_dir`. Each entry in `<<gen_role_name>>_configs` is a dict keyed by a label. The delivery mode is determined by which key is present:

```yaml
<<gen_role_name>>_configs:
  my_config:
    template: my_config.j2   # render a Jinja2 template from templates/
    file: /etc/app/config
    owner: root
    mode: "0644"
  another_config:
    content: "inline content" # write a literal string
    file: /etc/app/other
  third_config:
    src: files/config.conf    # copy a file from files/ without rendering
    file: /etc/app/third
```

Only one of `template`, `content`, or `src` should be set per entry. `owner`, `group`, and `mode` fall back to `site_config_owner`, `site_config_group`, and `site_config_mode` if not specified.

## Secrets

`tasks/secrets.yml` works identically to configs but with `no_log: true` on all tasks. Use `<<gen_role_name>>_secrets` and `<<gen_role_name>>_secrets_dir`.

